---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import releases from '../data/releases.json';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Getting Started with Lirune Reader — Windows & Android Guide"
  description="Step-by-step instructions for installing, configuring, and importing your books into Lirune Reader on Windows and Android."
>
  <div class="getting-started-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-header text-center">
        <span class="section-label">User Manual</span>
        <h1 class="page-title">Getting Started with Lirune</h1>
        <p class="page-subtitle mx-auto">
          Clear, step-by-step instructions to install Lirune Reader, import your personal documents, and customize your reading environment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Platform Jump -->
      <div class="jump-nav">
        <a href="#guide-windows" class="btn btn-secondary">Windows Desktop Guide ↓</a>
        <a href="#guide-android" class="btn btn-secondary">Android Mobile Guide ↓</a>
      </div>

      <!-- Windows Guide -->
      <section class="guide-block card" id="guide-windows">
        <div class="guide-header">
          <div class="guide-badge-group">
            <span class="badge badge-accent">Windows 10 & 11</span>
            <h2>Windows Quickstart Guide</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="guide-version">Latest Release: v{releases.windows.version}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-step">
          <div class="step-badge">Step 1</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Installation</h3>
            <p>You can choose between two convenient installation methods:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Microsoft Store (Recommended):</strong> Visit the <a href={releases.windows.storeUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link-inline">Lirune Reader Store Page</a> and click <em>Install</em>. Updates occur automatically in the background.</li>
              <li><strong>Direct NSIS Installer:</strong> Download <a href={releases.windows.installerUrl} class="link-inline"><code>{releases.windows.installerFilename}</code></a>, run the setup wizard, and launch Lirune from your Start Menu. If Windows SmartScreen prompts on unsigned GitHub binaries, click <em>More info</em> and <em>Run anyway</em>.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-step">
          <div class="step-badge">Step 2</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Importing Your Books</h3>
            <p>
              When Lirune starts, you are welcomed by a clean library drop-zone. You can add books immediately:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Drag & Drop:</strong> Drag single files or entire folders containing EPUB, PDF, MOBI, FB2, or CBZ books directly into the application window.</li>
              <li><strong>File Picker:</strong> Click the <strong>"+" Add Books</strong> button in the top-right toolbar to open the native Windows open file dialog.</li>
              <li>Lirune will automatically detect formats, parse metadata, extract cover art, and add each title to your library.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="guide-image-wrap">
              <img src="/images/screenshots/win-library-grid.png" alt="Library with imported books" width="800" height="450" loading="lazy" class="guide-img" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-step">
          <div class="step-badge">Step 3</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Reading & Layout Customization</h3>
            <p>
              Click any book card to open the reading interface:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Switch Layouts:</strong> Click the quick settings icon in the top toolbar to switch between <em>Two-Page Spread</em>, <em>Single Page</em>, or <em>Continuous Flow Scroll</em>.</li>
              <li><strong>Adjust Appearance:</strong> Choose between Dark, OLED, Light, Nord, or Sepia themes. Fine-tune your font size, line height, and margins to your liking.</li>
              <li><strong>Navigation:</strong> Open the Table of Contents drawer by pressing <kbd>T</kbd> or clicking the list icon. Search inside the book with <kbd>/</kbd>.</li>
              <li><strong>Fullscreen Immersion:</strong> Press <kbd>F11</kbd> to enter distraction-free fullscreen reading.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-step">
          <div class="step-badge">Step 4</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Library Backups</h3>
            <p>
              To back up your library metadata, bookmarks, highlights, and collections, open <strong>Settings → Storage & Maintenance</strong> and click <strong>Export Library Backup</strong>. This saves a portable JSON archive that you can restore anytime.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Android Guide -->
      <section class="guide-block card" id="guide-android">
        <div class="guide-header">
          <div class="guide-badge-group">
            <span class="badge badge-success">Android 8.0+</span>
            <h2>Android Quickstart Guide</h2>
          </div>
          <span class="guide-version">Latest Release: v{releases.android.version}</span>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-step">
          <div class="step-badge">Step 1</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Downloading & Sideloading the APK</h3>
            <p>
              Lirune for Android is distributed directly as an optimized, signed release APK:
            </p>
            <ol>
              <li>Download the official APK: <a href={releases.android.apkUrl} class="link-inline"><code>{releases.android.apkFilename}</code></a>.</li>
              <li>Open your device's <em>Downloads</em> folder and tap the APK file.</li>
              <li>If Android displays an <em>"Install unknown apps"</em> alert, tap <strong>Settings</strong>, toggle on permission for your browser or file manager, and return to complete installation.</li>
              <li>Tap <strong>Install</strong>, then tap <strong>Open</strong>.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-step">
          <div class="step-badge">Step 2</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Granting Folder Access via SAF</h3>
            <p>
              Lirune respects modern Android security and uses the official Storage Access Framework (SAF):
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Lirune will prompt you to select the folder where you store your digital books (e.g., your <code>Documents/Books</code> or <code>Download</code> directory).</li>
              <li>Select your folder and tap <strong>"Use this folder"</strong>.</li>
              <li>Lirune will scan the directory for supported formats without needing broad all-files storage permissions.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="guide-image-wrap">
              <img src="/images/screenshots/android-library.png" alt="Android library interface" width="320" height="500" loading="lazy" class="guide-img phone-size" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="guide-step">
          <div class="step-badge">Step 3</div>
          <div class="step-body">
            <h3>Reading with Scroll Engine v2</h3>
            <p>
              Tap any book to launch the reader. Lirune Android features exclusive Scroll Engine v2:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Continuous 60fps Scrolling:</strong> Swipe up or down smoothly. Content is dynamically virtualized for lightning-fast memory efficiency.</li>
              <li><strong>Touch Controls:</strong> Tap the center of the screen to reveal the reading controls header and bottom scrub bar.</li>
              <li><strong>Text-to-Speech:</strong> Tap the audio button to start offline TTS speech narration. You can regulate speed from 0.75x to 2.0x.</li>
              <li><strong>Table of Contents:</strong> Swipe in from the left or tap the TOC icon to jump directly across chapters.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .getting-started-page {
    padding-top: var(--sp-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-20);
  }

  .text-center { text-align: center; }
  .mx-auto { margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-8);
  }

  .page-title {
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .jump-nav {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--sp-4);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-12);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .guide-block {
    padding: var(--sp-10);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-16);
    background: var(--bg-surface);
  }

  .guide-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-end;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-8);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
  }

  .guide-badge-group {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
  }

  .guide-badge-group h2 {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
  }

  .guide-version {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .guide-step {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--sp-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-10);
  }

  .step-badge {
    background: var(--accent-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-accent);
    color: var(--accent-text);
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--r-full);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    height: fit-content;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .step-body {
    flex-grow: 1;
  }

  .step-body h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-2);
  }

  .step-body p {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .step-body ul, .step-body ol {
    padding-left: var(--sp-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .step-body strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .link-inline {
    color: var(--accent-chrome);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .guide-image-wrap {
    margin-top: var(--sp-4);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .guide-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .phone-size {
    max-width: 240px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  kbd {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--accent-chrome);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .guide-step {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--sp-3);
    }
  }
</style>
